</style>
</head>
<body>
<header><h1>🌐 Evolution of the Internet</h1><p>From early networks to a connected world.</p></header>
<main>
<article class="event"><p class="year">1960s–1970s</p><h2>Early Computer Networks</h2><p>Research networks helped establish ideas and technologies for connecting computers.</p></article>
<article class="event"><p class="year">1983</p><h2>TCP/IP Adoption</h2><p>ARPANET's transition to TCP/IP became an important milestone in internetworking.</p></article>
<article class="event"><p class="year">1989–1991</p><h2>World Wide Web</h2><p>Tim Berners-Lee proposed the Web and developed its early technologies for linked information.</p></article>
<article class="event"><p class="year">1990s</p><h2>Public Web Growth</h2><p>Web browsers and websites helped the internet reach more people.</p></article>
<article class="event"><p class="year">2000s</p><h2>Social and Interactive Web</h2><p>Blogs, social networks and online services encouraged people to create and share content.</p></article>
<article class="event"><p class="year">2010s–Today</p><h2>Mobile and Cloud Services</h2><p>Smartphones, streaming, cloud computing and AI-powered services continue to shape online experiences.</p></article>
</main>
<footer>The internet continues to evolve with new ideas and technologies. 🚀</footer>
